-- dnak: promoted from tools/spec_r542.json (the THE DSG DEEPEARTH AREAS 18-19, R542: printed pp. 90-91 (pdf 91-92) - the individual area key crosses the volcanic belt: Area 18 the Steam-Heated Caverns (the water-eroded cavern region altered by volcanic upheavals, its sharp fissures tapped into the caves; the meandering river from the Lower Lake reaching a connecting cavern five miles south, the source of a rapid hot stream that joins the river as the riverbed descends; the wide fine-sand shoreline landing for boats; the artificially expanded, straightened chute tunnel racing hot water into the river; the six large caves joined by narrow passages, steamy air, coated rock, boiling-to-cool pools and the slippery mildew; the north tunnel to Area 21 with its once-an-hour superheated blasts, 2% per round cumulative, 4d6 halved on a breath save; the east-tunnel stream inflicting 4d6 per round; the Plane of Fire spillover - efreet, fire elementals, salamanders, fire bats; the hell hounds, rats, green slime, crawlers and megalo centipedes; the fire giants holding sway, their nomadic clan numbering over 50; the half-usual fatigue in the muggy air; and the geysers - a 20% pool susceptibility, 6d6 halved on a save), and Area 19 the Chambers of Fire (the caves baked by the geothermal sources; the swept-clean approach tunnel at 1d6 per turn, dousing to avoid; the roughly circular caverns split by thousands-of-feet floor fissures belching smoke, poison gas, steam and fire once per hour at 25% per type for 1d6 rounds; the dangerous cave heat at 1d6 per round, halved by dousing; the eruption volley - 6d6 per round from steam or fire halved on a breath save, poison gas save-or-die, 1d4 turns of smoke at the page 36 effects; the slender stone arches at 50% over the 3d6-foot fissures; the four mephit forms at 50% after the matching eruption; the common fire bats; the diving magmen; the breathable but smoky air and the mildew; and the remote cavern where the toiling mephits widen the 20-foot fissure with their fireproof pickaxes, 21-40 of them entering per eruption, throwing intruders in as offerings to bring through a monstrously evil creature of the dark lower planes).);
-- DO NOT hand-edit; the spec JSON stays the adjudicated record.
return {
  "round" = 542,
  "prefix" = "dnak",
  "banner" = {
      "title" = "THE DSG DEEPEARTH AREAS 18-19, R542: printed pp. 90-91 (pdf 91-92) - the individual area key crosses the volcanic belt: Area 18 the Steam-Heated Caverns (the water-eroded cavern region altered by volcanic upheavals, its sharp fissures tapped into the caves; the meandering river from the Lower Lake reaching a connecting cavern five miles south, the source of a rapid hot stream that joins the river as the riverbed descends; the wide fine-sand shoreline landing for boats; the artificially expanded, straightened chute tunnel racing hot water into the river; the six large caves joined by narrow passages, steamy air, coated rock, boiling-to-cool pools and the slippery mildew; the north tunnel to Area 21 with its once-an-hour superheated blasts, 2% per round cumulative, 4d6 halved on a breath save; the east-tunnel stream inflicting 4d6 per round; the Plane of Fire spillover - efreet, fire elementals, salamanders, fire bats; the hell hounds, rats, green slime, crawlers and megalo centipedes; the fire giants holding sway, their nomadic clan numbering over 50; the half-usual fatigue in the muggy air; and the geysers - a 20% pool susceptibility, 6d6 halved on a save), and Area 19 the Chambers of Fire (the caves baked by the geothermal sources; the swept-clean approach tunnel at 1d6 per turn, dousing to avoid; the roughly circular caverns split by thousands-of-feet floor fissures belching smoke, poison gas, steam and fire once per hour at 25% per type for 1d6 rounds; the dangerous cave heat at 1d6 per round, halved by dousing; the eruption volley - 6d6 per round from steam or fire halved on a breath save, poison gas save-or-die, 1d4 turns of smoke at the page 36 effects; the slender stone arches at 50% over the 3d6-foot fissures; the four mephit forms at 50% after the matching eruption; the common fire bats; the diving magmen; the breathable but smoky air and the mildew; and the remote cavern where the toiling mephits widen the 20-foot fissure with their fireproof pickaxes, 21-40 of them entering per eruption, throwing intruders in as offerings to bring through a monstrously evil creature of the dark lower planes).",
      "provenance" = "the DSG scan (archive.org item advanced-dungeons-dragons-1st-edition), pdf = printed + 1; the text read from the IA djvu OCR (djvu.txt lines ~11485-11685) with the pdf Acrobat-Capture layer as the second read (idx 206 and 208 = the printed pp. 90-91 windows); the compiled-tables appendix has no reprint of this prose. A CLEAN-READ ROUND: both machine reads agree on every load-bearing number - the five-mile junction, the six caves, the 2%-cumulative blast with its 4d6, the 4d6 stream, the 50-giant clan, the 20%/6d6 geysers, the 1d6-per-turn tunnel, the 25% eruption types lasting 1d6 rounds, the 1d6-per-round caves, the 6d6 steam-or-fire, the 1d4-turn smoke, the 50% arches over the 3d6-foot fissures, the four mephit forms at 50%, and the 21-40 (1d20+20) toiling mephits widening the 20-foot fissure; the only garbles settled cross-read (the djvu 296 and 346-foot garbles for the capture 2% and 3d6, the capture ld6/ld4/ld20+20 for the djvu 1d6 and 1d4 and 1d20+20). SEAMS: the R518 water travel (the river junction and the chute), the Monster Manual denizens (the efreet, salamanders, hell hounds, fire giants, mephits, magmen and lava children to come in Area 20), the PHB fire resistance and breath saves, and the page 36 smoke rules. A ZERO-FLIP ROUND: the pp. 75-98 Deepearth child remains open until the setting lands in full (the R527/R533-R541 precedent - the gap report is NOT in the git add). Nothing auto-credits.",
      "sentinel" = "A procedural-plus-prose round: no tables pin. The numbers pin as consts per the R508 convention - the junction miles, the cave count, the blast base and step percentages, the dice of the blast, stream and geyser damage, the giant clan size, the fatigue divisor, the geyser pool percentage, the tunnel and cave damage dice, the eruption type percentage and rounds, the eruption damage dice, the smoke turns, the arch percentage, the fissure width dice, the mephit forms and follow percentage, and the toiling-mephit count with its sides and base and the 20-foot fissure width, with the 4d6, 6d6, 1d6, 1d4, 3d6 and 1d20+20 dice pinned as count-sides(-multiplier/base) const pairs or triples. The geography, denizens, resources and unique-features prose pins as bools for both areas. The water-travel/MM/PHB seams are noted; the Deepearth child stays open; nothing auto-credits.",
    },
  "consts" = { {
